name sat-03-escort-shield-1
timeout 520
time 1991-01-19T08:00:00Z
wx fixture wx-2026-07-27T00Z.wxb

# MEASURING RIG, NOT A CAMPAIGN RUNG. `sat-*` files belong to no `.fbc`, are named by no campaign and
# move no doctrine. They exist because 33 of the 34 campaign cells are NOT GRADUABLE: their outcome
# class (V, M) — fb_fitness.side_key, summed over the declared side — does not move when the doctrine
# genome moves, so no doctrine shift can be demonstrated on them. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# WHAT HOLDS THIS CELL AT THE TIPPING POINT: THE ESCORT'S OBJECTIVE IS SOMEBODY ELSE'S SURVIVAL.
# Each of the four escorts declares `objective protect unit <ONE named striker>` — "the named unit is
# still combat-effective at the END of the run" (core/FBObjective.h) — and the four names are the four
# aircraft of the package it covers. An escort therefore cannot score by killing MiG-29s; it scores only
# if the ONE jet it was given comes home. That is a different question from every campaign rung, all of
# which grade an escort on `kill team hostile`: one bit for a whole flight, moved by no lever in the file.
#
# THE RATIO IS THE THRESHOLD, [SET] at 1.5: SIX interceptors against FOUR escorts, in two groups of three
# on separated bearings. Below 1.0 the screen holds by arithmetic and doctrine cannot show; at 1.5 it has
# to CHOOSE, and `pilot/FBFlightPicture::Assign` makes that choice out of a shared picture whose contents
# depend on where the wingmen are standing — which is exactly `pilot_flight_spread_frac`/`_trail_frac`/
# `_stack_frac`. The two groups are separated by 0.24 deg of latitude (about 27 km) so that a four-ship
# at `shape-wide` (2.5 x 1 852 m of lateral step, 23 km from position 3 to position 5) spans BOTH and one
# at `shape-tight` (0.35 -> 648 m, 3.2 km overall) spans neither.
#
# AND A SECOND, INDEPENDENT THRESHOLD ON THE SAME FOUR ESCORTS, because one axis is not a gradient:
# `sa6`'s EnvAltMaxM = 7 000 m (core/FBSite.h) against a screen whose lead sits at 6 000 m and whose
# station steps by `pilot_flight_stack_frac x FormationStackM` = frac x 150 m (doc/formation.md 4.2).
# [DERIVED] baseline 6 000 / 6 150 / 6 300 / 6 450 — all four inside the envelope; `shape-stacked` (3.0)
# 6 000 / 6 450 / 6 900 / 7 350 — the fourth is 350 m above it. `zone sa6belt` carries the battery's own
# EnvMaxM (22 000 m) and EnvAltMinM/EnvAltMaxM (100 / 7 000 m), so the volume the objective names and the
# volume the missile works in are ONE BODY. `exposure 200` is [SET] in a MEASURED GAP: [MESS] the belt
# dwell over the lever set falls in clusters at 116 .. 168 s and 240 .. 250 s, and 200 s lies in the 72 s
# between them, so no member sits within 30 s of its own verdict.
#
# EVERY HOSTILE AIRCRAFT IS NAMED by an escort's `kill unit` (ee1 takes ia1 and ib1, ee2 ia2 and ib2,
# ee3 ia3, ee4 ib3). That is not scorekeeping: an actor's loss ends the run unless another actor DECLARED
# an objective covering it (doc/missions/runtime.md, `ExpectedLoss`), and without the six names one CAP
# kill would cut the run at the instant it happened.
#
# THE RELEASE HALF is a CCIP pair beside the CCRP package, and it is here because `pilot_attack_bias_s`
# and `pilot_attack_ccip_m` need a ground half of their own: [MESS] the package's Mk 84 CCRP passes land
# 55 .. 62 m long, inside the Mk 84's 100 m fail radius under every bias allele, so the package alone
# reports both genes inert. The pair carries Mk 82 (fail radius 45 m, [MESS] mk82-radius.fbm) and flies
# CCIP, because `pilot_attack_ccip_m` is read ONLY in `FBDeliveryMode::Ccip`. `etgte` is placed 72.7 m
# BEYOND its striker's steerpoint so its baseline impact falls SHORT and `bias-early` is the allele that
# loses it, while `etgtf` sits on the steerpoint and `bias-late` is the allele that loses that one.
#
# GENE FAMILIES, LIVE AND INERT — stated in advance, then measured (the arena's own table, 25 levers):
#   live    G1 shape 6 of 6:  shape-abreast (26,24)  shape-trail (24,19)  shape-tight (26,24)
#                             shape-wide (27,25)  shape-flat (26,23)  shape-stacked (25,23)
#   live    G6 bias  3 of 3:  bias-early (23,18)  bias-late (23,19)  bias-rail (18,13)
#   live    G7 ccip  1 of 2:  ccip-tight (23,18);  ccip-open INERT
#   live    G3 net   1 of 2:  net-off (23,21);  `sort-left`/`sort-near` are dead text beside a live net
#   live    G5 emcon 1 of 3:  emcon-wide (26,24);  emcon-tight/mid INERT
#   INERT   G2 cover 0 of 3:  the AIM-120 binds 0.3 s — `flt_defer_s` = 0 in 2 464 runs on 154 cells
#   INERT   G4 energy 0 of 3: it lives only inside `Phase::Bfm`, and no unit here flies `set task bfm`
#   BASELINE (24, 20).  12 movers of 24, 11 of them excluding the broken `bias-rail` stop; 10 distinct
#   classes — the widest spread of the three rigs; modal share 52.0 % (13 of 25). S1 and S2 both hold.
#
# S7, AND IT IS REPORTED HERE BECAUSE IT DID NOT PASS: [MESS] 4 of 8 spawn perturbations on the 0.8 m
# grid flip the baseline class — the worst of the three rigs, and the cause is STRUCTURAL and belongs to
# the question, not to a coordinate. `protect` is answered at the END of the run (it is deferred, like
# `survive`), and [MESS] the baseline run does NOT reach its timeout: `emib1` is killed at t = 270.8 s,
# `ee1` at 271.4 and `ee3` at 281.6, and the run is cut at t = 301.7 when `emib1`'s wreck reaches the
# ground (`FirstFlightKo`, doc/missions/runtime.md). An end-referenced objective on a run whose end is an
# EVENT is chaos-sensitive by construction. The way out is not a coordinate tweak: it is either an
# objective kind with a time window (doc/missions/verdict.md books its absence as a deliberate gap) or a
# question that is not end-referenced — which is what sat-02-picture-split is, and it flips 0 of 8.
# This file is kept as it is because the escort question is worth measuring and because a measured
# failure is knowledge; it must NOT be fed to an evolution until S7 holds.
#
# THE ARENA: ten F-16 — a four-ship escort screen, the four-ship package it covers, and a CCIP pair —
# against six MiG-29 under a GCI brief, one SA-6 and its EW radar. `--elev const`, 0 m datum, no terrain
# masking (C4). Every coordinate is [SET]. `wx fixture` is the committed GFS blob. Day, 11:00 local, sun
# about +33 deg [DERIVED] — the merge is EYED, deliberately: a night merge removes sensors/FBVisualSystem
# from the picture and with it one of the inputs the screen competes for.
# THE SUBSTITUTION AND ITS DIRECTION: the MiG-29 is the strongest Soviet-pattern fighter in the tree, so
# RED is stronger here than any historical six-ship this geometry resembles. No claim is made that it
# resembles one — this file is an instrument, not a rung.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WITH SIX INTERCEPTORS AGAINST A FOUR-SHIP SCREEN, DOES THE SCREEN'S OWN
# SHAPE DECIDE WHICH OF ITS FOUR CHARGES COMES HOME?
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   telemetry_ee*.csv  `flt_src`, `flt_assign`, `flt_switch`, `flt_dup` — the screen's sort at 1.5
#                      contacts per shooter; `zone_sa6belt_s` — the dwell the stack gene moves
#   telemetry_ep*.csv  the package: who was still combat-effective at the end
#   telemetry_ec*.csv  the CCIP pair: `releases`, `aimErrM` against a 45 m radius
#   events.log         `mission OBJECTIVE unit=ee* kind="protect unit ..."` — the four bits that matter,
#                      `flight SORT_ASSIGN` per member and tick, `sms LAUNCH_SOLUTION` per shooter
#
# READING RULE, BINDING: exit 1 = FAIL and exit 3 = TIMEOUT are BOTH expected and NEITHER is the
# measurement; an escort whose charge was lost reports its own `protect` VIOLATED while still flying,
# which is the point of the kind. THE MEASUREMENT IS (V, M) SUMMED OVER THE TEN F-16 — six `kill unit` on
# the CAP, four `protect`, four `avoid zone`, six `kill unit` on aim points and ten `survive`, 30
# objectives — AND ITS SPREAD ACROSS THE LEVER SET. A reader who reports how many MiG-29s were shot down
# has answered a question this file does not ask: a screen that kills four and loses its package scores
# ZERO here. And because S7 fails, a reader must treat any SINGLE run of this file as noise.

zone sa6belt 33.20000 44.30000 22000 100 7000

unit sa6bat
  module sa6
  team hostile
  spawn 33.20000 44.30000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free

unit ewnode
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 33.35000 44.10000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free

unit ee1
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight ea 1
  spawn 33.20000 43.90000 6000 90.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set datalink on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 33.20000 45.20000 6000 480
  objective kill unit emia1
  objective kill unit emib1
  objective protect unit ep1
  objective avoid zone sa6belt exposure 200
  objective survive

